Package: vayuayan
Type: Package
Title: Air Quality Data from Indian Monitoring Networks and Satellites
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Saket", "Choudhary", , "saketc@iitb.ac.in", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Mahesh Kumar", "Prajapat", , "22b0433@iitb.ac.in", role = "aut"),
    person("Darakhshan", "Nehal", , "darakhshannehal@gmail.com", role = "ctb")
  )
Description: Download and analyze air pollution data from three sources.
    The Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) of India publishes historical
    and real-time particulate matter and air quality index readings from
    more than 600 continuous ambient air quality monitoring stations
    <https://airquality.cpcb.gov.in/ccr/>. Open Air Quality (OAQ) aggregates
    low-cost sensor networks in India. The Atmospheric Composition Analysis
    Group at Washington University in St. Louis provides satellite-derived
    fine particulate matter (PM2.5) estimates at 0.01 degree resolution
    for 1998-2024 <https://www.satpm.org>. Includes station lookup,
    nearest-station matching, the CPCB National Air Quality Index computed
    from pollutant concentrations, and regional PM2.5 summaries from
    'NetCDF' rasters. An R port of the 'vayuayan' 'Python' package.
